    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know, i know. talking to a therapist is the \"correct\" answer. but it feels so small compared to this. it's like trying to put a band-aid on a void. everything i do is just staying alive so i can do more of the same thing tomorrow. just more noise, more emptiness. why is the only way to actually find peace to keep struggling against something that's clearly already won? it feels like the only real way to get some actual, true silence is to just stop everything. permanently.",
